course: dictionary
lesson: 11903
title: One word, many faces
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can mean more than one thing. The words around them, the context, show you which meaning the writer wants. «The weather bulletin said heavy rain was coming tonight.» The words weather and rain show that bulletin means a short official notice about something important.
explain: «Mum listened to the news bulletin on the radio before breakfast.» News and radio tell you this bulletin is a short news report. Ask yourself, where would I find this? That question often gives you the meaning straight away.
explain: «The school bulletin came home in my bag, with the club news and the sports results.» Here bulletin means a short printed newsletter. Check by swapping in a word: does newsletter still make sense in the sentence? It does, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: A bulletin is a short report or notice, not a long story.
fact: A bulletin can be a short news report on TV, radio or online.
fact: A bulletin can also be a short printed newsletter from a school, club or group.
fact: An official bulletin is a short notice about something important, such as the weather or someone's health.
fact: In an emergency, bulletins warn people about storms or floods. A bulletin board is a board where notices are pinned up.
exercise: «The weather bulletin warned of strong winds and flooding.» What is a bulletin in this sentence? | A kind of cake | A long story in a book | *A short official notice about something important | A game played in the park
exercise: «The school bulletin has the club news and the sports results.» What is a bulletin here? | A type of tent | A pair of muddy shoes | *A short printed newsletter | A large bell in the hall
exercise: «Mum listened to the news bulletin on the radio.» Find and copy one word that tells you the bulletin is a news report. | Mum | *news | breakfast | listened
test: Sam says a bulletin is a kind of biscuit. What is the right meaning? | A loud noise from a drum | A type of walking shoe | *A short news report, a newsletter or an official notice | A sweet biscuit with jam
test: «The bulletin board in the hall has a notice about the school trip.» What is a bulletin board? | A board for playing chess | A soft cushion for the bench | *A board where notices are pinned up | A table for lunch
exam: Which sentence uses bulletin to mean a short official notice about someone's health? | «We danced a bulletin all night at the party.» | «The bulletin was made of soft wood and painted green.» | «The bulletin raced the dog across the park.» | *«The hospital bulletin said the patient was resting comfortably.»
